### Real-Time Food Delivery Updates - demo requests
### Import into Postman as raw text, or run each block with the VS Code
### "REST Client" extension, or copy the curl commands below.

### 1. Create an order (published as PLACED)
POST http://localhost:4000/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "restaurantId": "resto-1",
  "customerId": "cust-1",
  "items": ["Pad Thai", "Thai Iced Tea"]
}

### 2. Restaurant confirms the order
PATCH http://localhost:4000/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "CONFIRMED"
}

### 3. Restaurant marks the order ready for pickup
### -> this is the exact moment from the proposal's pain point:
###    the rider service used to find out late or not at all
PATCH http://localhost:4000/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "READY_FOR_PICKUP"
}

### 4. A rider picks the order up
PATCH http://localhost:4000/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PICKED_UP",
  "riderId": "rider-9"
}

### 5. Order delivered
PATCH http://localhost:4000/orders/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "DELIVERED"
}

### --- Now check that every downstream service learned about it independently ---

### Customer app feed
GET http://localhost:4001/feed/cust-1

### Rider pickup pool (should be empty again after PICKED_UP)
GET http://localhost:4002/pickup-pool

### Notification log
GET http://localhost:4003/notifications
